s://semgrep.dev/blog/2026/we-have-mythos-at-home-glm-52-beats-claude-in-our=
-cyber-benchmarks)
Semgrep=E2=80=99s [Katie Paxton-Fear](https://www.linkedin.com/in/katiepf/)=
, [Seth Jaksik](https://www.linkedin.com/in/sethjaksik/), [Brenden Noblitt]=
(https://www.linkedin.com/in/brendennoblitt/), and [Erik Buchanan](https://=
www.linkedin.com/in/erikbuchanan/) benchmarked GLM 5.2, an open-weight mode=
l from Zhipu AI, against their IDOR detection dataset using only a basic Py=
dantic AI harness and prompt, finding it achieved 39% F1 score and beat Cla=
ude Code (32%) at roughly $0.17 per vulnerability found, though it still tr=
ailed Semgrep's multimodal pipeline with endpoint discovery scaffolding (53=
-61% F1, top with GPT 5.5).

=F0=9F=92=A1 I like posts comparing various models and vanilla models vs mo=
del + harnesses. It=E2=80=99d be interesting to know more about the dataset=
 though- languages/frameworks in use, how many examples, etc.=20



[Snyk VulnBench JS 1.0: Can LLMs Find the Same Bugs Twice?](https://snyk.io=
/blog/snyk-vulnbench-js-1-0-llm-security-review-repeatability)
Snyk's [Liran Tal](https://www.linkedin.com/in/talliran/) describes evaluat=
ing Snyk=E2=80=99s VulnBench JS 1.0 (10 JavaScript fixtures with 44 Snyk Co=
de reference findings, each a small Express-based application) across 300 v=
ulnerability scans on  (10 fixtures =C3=97 6 configurations =C3=97 5 repeti=
tions) to measure LLM security review repeatability against Snyk Code SAST =
as a deterministic reference. As you=E2=80=99d expect, the post found resul=
ts vary across different LLM-only scans.

=F0=9F=92=A1 This kind of felt like a puff piece. Of course a deterministic=
 static analysis scan in this setup will be a) faster and b) more consisten=
t than an LLM-based approach. Also, it=E2=80=99s no surprise that a product=
 performs well on simple, small applications it was already tested on. A mo=
re representative benchmark would be testing on complex, real-world applica=
tions, or at least ones that the product hasn=E2=80=99t already been tuned =
on. If they released the benchmark apps + reproduction code that would be c=
ool though.




